barev-purple (1.6) unstable; urgency=low

  * fixing barev contact field disappearing from osso-abook contact page:
    bare-nick buddies (without ipv6 in the name) never had the NO_SAVE flag
    cleared in barev_add_buddy. on haze restart or account toggle the buddy
    was absent from blist.xml, haze removed it from mission control, and
    osso-abook dropped the eds field. unconditionally clearing NO_SAVE for
    all manually-added buddies so they survive restarts. also guarding
    against haze re-calling add_buddy on reconnect overwriting existing
    protocol_data with a fresh empty struct.

 -- Norayr Chilingarian <norayr@arnet.am>  Mon, 07 Jul 2026 02:30:00 +0000

barev-purple (1.5) unstable; urgency=low

  * adding diagnostic logging for second-connection failure: parse_from logs
    the incoming from_jid and buddy match result, stream_started logs entry
    state and when the fully_sent block fires, barev_send_current_presence
    logs the account status being sent. adding defensive retry in
    barev_auto_connect_timer: when a connection is alive but ping never
    started (fully_sent block never ran), stream_started is called again to
    send presence.

 -- Norayr Chilingarian <norayr@arnet.am>  Mon, 07 Jul 2026 00:30:00 +0000

barev-purple (1.4) unstable; urgency=low

  * fixing second and subsequent connections failing to send presence: when
    bonjour_find_buddy_by_localpart returns null due to ambiguous localpart
    (both 'inky' and 'inky@ip' in blist), conv_match_by_ip is called and
    clears bconv->buddy_name internally. the second validate_ip_consistency
    call in conv_match_by_name then receives a null jid and returns false,
    closing a perfectly valid incoming connection. stream was sent but
    presence was never delivered so the peer never appeared online. fixed by
    preserving bconv->buddy_name across both conv_match_by_ip call sites
    in conv_match_by_name so the jid fallback works for bare-nick buddies.

 -- Norayr Chilingarian <norayr@arnet.am>  Sun, 06 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000

